<title>BELGIUM: EU holds 1.18 million tonnes grain in public stores.</title>
<headline>EU holds 1.18 million tonnes grain in public stores.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union intervention grain stocks stood at 1.18 million tonnes on April 6, compared with 2.60 million tonnes at the start of 1996/97 (July/June), according to European Commission figures released on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The total included 314,263 tonnes of intervention soft wheat, compared with 458,970 tonnes at the start of the season.</p>
<p>Intervention barley totalled 370,104 tonnes, against 1.34 million tonnes on July 1, 1996.</p>
<p>A further 492,412 tonnes of rye was held in EU intervention stores, against 793,261 tonnes last July.</p>
<p>Intervention maize stocks stood at 1,701 tonnes, compared with three tonnes over the same period.</p>
<p>European Union intervention grain stocks (000 tonnes)</p>
<p>		     6/4/97		   1/7/96</p>
<p> All cereals     1,178,462		2,596,112</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p> Soft wheat	  314,263		  458,970</p>
<p> Durum wheat	    nil		     nil</p>
<p> Barley		370,104		1,343,870</p>
<p> Rye		   492,412		  793,761</p>
<p> Maize		   1,701			  3</p>
<p> Sorghum		  nil		     nil</p>
<p> Triticale		nil		     nil</p>
<p>NB: Figures are net after deduction of domestic and export sales commitments</p>
</text>
